{"q": 19177, "quiz": 1511, "obj": "P2.WORD_CONTEXT", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "The book uses the word \"rare\" about bears. What does \"rare\" mean here?", "why": "المعنى من السياق القريب: الدببة «apex predators»، وقبلها «An apex predator does not often get eaten by other animals.» ثم «It’s rare for another animal to catch and eat a bear!»", "opts": [{"t": "It is good for the bear.", "dx": "JUMP", "key": false}, {"t": "It does not happen often.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "It happens every day.", "dx": "REV", "key": false}, {"t": "It is easy for big animals.", "dx": "JUMP", "key": false}]},
{"q": 19178, "quiz": 1511, "obj": "P4.FIT", "kind": "mcq", "was": "judge", "body": "Is \"Links in the Food Chain\" a good name for this book?", "why": "العنوان يفي بما في النص: «Each living thing is a link in the food chain.» ثم تتوالى الحلقات واحدة بعد أخرى حتى «The last link in a food chain is called an apex predator.»", "opts": [{"t": "No. The book says nothing about food.", "dx": "REV", "key": false}, {"t": "No. The book is only about bears and foxes.", "dx": "PART", "key": false}, {"t": "Yes. The book goes from link to link in a food chain.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "Yes. The book is about a real chain around a bear.", "dx": "LITR", "key": false}]},
{"q": 19167, "quiz": 1510, "obj": "P1.COMPETITOR", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "How do fish get oxygen from the water?", "why": "في النص أعضاء عدّة تتنافس (القشور والزعانف والرئتان)، والمطلوب عضو التنفس: «They use these gills to breathe in the oxygen they need from water.»", "opts": [{"t": "With their scales.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}, {"t": "With their lungs.", "dx": "REV", "key": false}, {"t": "With their fins.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}, {"t": "With their gills.", "dx": null, "key": true}]},
{"q": 19168, "quiz": 1510, "obj": "P2.UNSIGNALLED", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "Fish and mammals sleep in different ways. What is different for fish?", "why": "السبب في الجملة التالية بلا أداة ربط بينهما: «Fish do not sleep in the same way mammals sleep.» ثم «Fish can't close their eyes because they don't have eyelids.»", "opts": [{"t": "They never sleep or rest.", "dx": "REV", "key": false}, {"t": "Their eyes stay open in their sleep.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "They close their eyes at night.", "dx": "REV", "key": false}, {"t": "They sleep only in big schools.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}]},
{"q": 19169, "quiz": 1510, "obj": "P1.COMPETITOR", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "How do scales help fish?", "why": "في النص وظائف عدّة تتنافس، والمطلوب وظيفة القشور: «The scales help fish move easily through the water.»", "opts": [{"t": "They help fish find a place to hide.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}, {"t": "They help fish breathe in oxygen.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}, {"t": "They help fish move easily through the water.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "They help fish close their eyes.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}]},
